1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,512
This project asks whether a configurable Bitcoin strategy improves returns and
drawdown relative to simpler alternatives.

2
00:00:08,512 --> 00:00:12,099
We assume Bitcoin remains operational and tradable.

3
00:00:12,099 --> 00:00:14,491
We do not assume it is profitable.

4
00:00:14,491 --> 00:00:16,882
All funds and fills are simulated.

5
00:00:16,882 --> 00:00:23,987
The project separates historical research, an operational paper engine, and a
prospective evaluation.

6
00:00:23,987 --> 00:00:30,459
This walkthrough follows the money and explains the evidence, including unfavorable
results.

7
00:00:30,459 --> 00:00:34,943
The account starts with ten thousand dollars and zero Bitcoin.

8
00:00:34,943 --> 00:00:43,333
In a bullish regime, five thousand dollars is assigned to DCA, three thousand to
swing, and two thousand to reserve.

9
00:00:43,333 --> 00:00:47,094
These are budget targets, not immediate investments.

10
00:00:47,094 --> 00:00:48,613
DCA spends gradually.

11
00:00:48,613 --> 00:00:55,918
Swing needs its own entry conditions and is disabled in this forward run, so its
money stays in cash.

12
00:00:55,918 --> 00:01:02,428
Budget reviews consider existing holdings and pending orders before moving available
cash.

13
00:01:02,428 --> 00:01:07,560
Daily trend compares the closing price with its two hundred day average.

14
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:10,839
Momentum measures the return over thirty days.

15
00:01:10,839 --> 00:01:17,397
Both positive conditions identify a bullish regime; both negative identify a bearish
regime.

16
00:01:17,397 --> 00:01:21,674
Large daily true ranges can select a high volatility regime.

17
00:01:21,674 --> 00:01:24,882
Hourly indicators use only completed candles.

18
00:01:24,882 --> 00:01:29,088
Breakout and volume references exclude the decision candle.

19
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:35,931
Missing hours are recorded rather than invented, and short hourly indicators restart
after gaps.

20
00:01:35,931 --> 00:01:44,799
With a five thousand dollar DCA reference, a two percent tranche gives a purchase
budget of one hundred dollars, including fees.

21
00:01:44,799 --> 00:01:49,371
A scheduled purchase is due approximately every twenty four hours.

22
00:01:49,371 --> 00:01:56,022
A completed hourly close at least three percent below the last actual DCA fill can
also qualify.

23
00:01:56,022 --> 00:02:01,218
Both routes share a twelve hour cooldown and the same rolling spending cap.

24
00:02:01,218 --> 00:02:06,691
Fourteen percent of the reference allows seven hundred dollars over seven days.

25
00:02:06,691 --> 00:02:11,610
The engine also checks available cash, valid data and portfolio limits.

26
00:02:11,610 --> 00:02:15,828
A buy starts from the observed ask and adds adverse slippage.

27
00:02:15,828 --> 00:02:18,871
A sell starts from the bid and subtracts it.

28
00:02:18,871 --> 00:02:25,787
The simulation assumes zero point six percent fees and zero point one percent
slippage on each fill.

29
00:02:25,787 --> 00:02:30,075
These are experimental costs, not a verified account fee tier.

30
00:02:30,075 --> 00:02:35,401
Decimal arithmetic and conservative rounding keep money and quantity precise.

31
00:02:35,401 --> 00:02:39,758
Pending buys reserve cash, and pending sells reserve inventory.

32
00:02:39,758 --> 00:02:45,498
Immutable fills allow an independent reconstruction of the account after a restart.

33
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:53,806
The candidate swing entry looks for upward trend, a breakout above the previous
twenty hours, and elevated volume.

34
00:02:53,806 --> 00:02:56,867
ATR measures movement size, not direction.

35
00:02:56,867 --> 00:03:03,280
Position sizing begins with a planned loss budget of half a percent of portfolio
equity.

36
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:06,413
The stop is one point five ATR below entry.

37
00:03:06,413 --> 00:03:11,296
The profit target must cover costs and twice the modeled stop loss.

38
00:03:11,296 --> 00:03:14,648
A target more than eight ATR away is rejected.

39
00:03:14,648 --> 00:03:22,446
These filters do not prove profitability, and the current forward experiment leaves
swing entries disabled.

40
00:03:22,446 --> 00:03:32,076
The offline research compares forty seven distinct profiles across allocations, dip
thresholds, volatility multipliers and defensive exits.

41
00:03:32,076 --> 00:03:36,025
It uses twenty three nonoverlapping development episodes.

42
00:03:36,025 --> 00:03:40,044
Each fit sees only outcomes already complete at that date.

43
00:03:40,044 --> 00:03:45,240
The score rewards mean logarithmic return and subtracts a drawdown penalty.

44
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:50,090
That penalty expresses a declared preference, not a universal optimum.

45
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:57,157
A context model needs enough matching earlier episodes and otherwise falls back to
the global ranking.

46
00:03:57,157 --> 00:03:58,750
Cash is a valid winner.

47
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:03,253
This search is not continuously retuning the operational account.

48
00:04:03,253 --> 00:04:12,797
In the frozen historical holdout, feature allocation returned fourteen point three
seven percent with fourteen point six six percent maximum drawdown.

49
00:04:12,797 --> 00:04:19,287
Buy and hold returned nine point eight two percent with twenty nine point four eight
percent drawdown.

50
00:04:19,287 --> 00:04:25,014
However, the longer development selector reached seventy two point three percent
drawdown.

51
00:04:25,014 --> 00:04:30,422
The initial swing rule lost twenty point six four percent in the holdout after costs.

52
00:04:30,422 --> 00:04:36,275
These limitations are why the historical winner was not simply promoted into live
operation.

53
00:04:36,275 --> 00:04:42,065
The holdout is now observed and cannot become a fresh independent test for later
revisions.

54
00:04:42,065 --> 00:04:47,049
Pausing purchases alone leaves previously accumulated Bitcoin exposed.

55
00:04:47,049 --> 00:04:51,605
The operational policy can request exits from existing holdings.

56
00:04:51,605 --> 00:04:58,084
New purchases respect a sixty percent Bitcoin exposure cap and twenty percent minimum
cash.

57
00:04:58,084 --> 00:05:03,138
Price appreciation can trigger a trim above sixty two percent exposure.

58
00:05:03,138 --> 00:05:09,190
Rapid decline, confirmed bearish days and portfolio drawdown can request liquidation.

59
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:12,820
The original capital floor can halt the experiment.

60
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:16,807
Recovery requires cooldown and distinct qualifying days.

61
00:05:16,807 --> 00:05:22,787
A price gap or unavailable market can still produce a worse exit than the threshold.

62
00:05:22,787 --> 00:05:28,578
The forward experiment starts fresh accounts for the candidate and three comparison
books.

63
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:32,824
Each receives the same prospective observations and modeled costs.

64
00:05:32,824 --> 00:05:39,258
All seven anchored twenty four hour days must reach at least ninety nine percent
quote age coverage.

65
00:05:39,258 --> 00:05:43,955
The earlier window failed after a long interruption and remains archived.

66
00:05:43,955 --> 00:05:52,963
A separate recovery rehearsal confirmed that Task Scheduler can replace a stopped
supervisor without changing balances or duplicating fills.

67
00:05:52,963 --> 00:05:57,596
Historical warm up and artificial tests never count as prospective days.

68
00:05:57,596 --> 00:06:01,521
The replacement forward run is still collecting observations.

69
00:06:01,521 --> 00:06:05,896
There are no completed conclusions about its investment performance.

70
00:06:05,896 --> 00:06:11,107
The video will be regenerated with the actual results after the full week passes.

71
00:06:11,107 --> 00:06:14,824
The README provides setup and reproduction commands.

72
00:06:14,824 --> 00:06:20,183
The formula guide connects reported values to equations and saved examples.

73
00:06:20,183 --> 00:06:30,331
The final evaluation includes daily coverage, independent ledger reconciliation,
source and configuration checksums, and strategy comparisons.

74
00:06:30,331 --> 00:06:36,406
Tests cover accounting, causality, restart behavior, risk controls and release gates.

75
00:06:36,406 --> 00:06:42,623
Real messaging, paid model calls and Docker execution remain unverified optional
paths.

76
00:06:42,623 --> 00:06:47,697
A successful week establishes behavior under those observed conditions.

77
00:06:47,697 --> 00:06:54,343
It does not establish durable investment performance or a personal allocation
recommendation.
